      NetHack development does not use SourceForge at all.
They are only used to host the present incarnation of the
nethack.org web site.  Whoever modified the nethack project
page there did so without devteam's consent, and either
managed to do so without having admin access to the project
or persuaded sourceforge to grant admin access without
consulting the existing admin users.

      The development code for whichever version eventually
comes next is still entirely in C, except for the couple of
front ends (BeOS and Qt, I think) which are already using some
C++.  There are no plans to rewrite nethack in some other
language nor to tack on new bits written in other languages.


